comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-15T13:55:57.823Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status search and targeted release, immutability, isImmutable, tag, asset, and attestation searches found release reliability, signing, provenance, and one-per-day owners but no item that owns GitHub's platform immutable-release setting or requires isImmutable=true. This issue is limited to that missing enforcement and verification contract; it does not duplicate signing, npm provenance, release recovery, or manual same-day policy work."
  "2026-08-15T14:07:05.203Z","harness:codex","Linked verification executed on 2026-08-15: npm registry version check passed; GitHub release query executed successfully and returned the current release state, which remains isImmutable:false by design of this open issue. The test proves the observation path is executable; the future gate must additionally assert true after policy enablement and carry a seeded false-state negative control."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-15T13:55:57.823Z","harness:codex","Primary evidence: gh release list reports the sole v2026.8.15 record with isImmutable:false. GitHub's official immutable-release documentation states that the repository setting applies to future releases, locks associated tags and assets, and creates a release attestation; therefore existing releases must not be rewritten or republished to simulate compliance."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-15T13:55:57.823Z","harness:codex","A unique tag and package plus a successful workflow prove publication identity, but they do not prove platform immutability. Treat GitHub's immutable bit and attestation as separate supply-chain evidence, and perform asset assembly before publication."
